Smarduch Mario-CMS063 wrote:
> Hi,
>     I'm relatively new to Linux maillists and proceedngs although not so
> kernel development. I'm wondering what is a procedure for proposing
> kernel enhancements in Linux. There are several that we're using at
> Motorola (some are CGL related) and we would like see if such enhancements may be 
> considered for kernel inclusion.

1. Read the procedure at Documentation/SubmittingPatches and probably
Documentation/CodingStyle at the root source of kernel. Send it to
Linus, don't use attachement.

2. Wait and hope that Linus will agree with your patch, or if your patch
 took so long, just begin the discussion on lkml about your changes.
